blocks.prompt:
Consider the following loop:
```
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    int x = a * b;
    arr[i] = x + i;
}
```
Identify and move the loop-invariant computation.

steps.text:
Move the invariant computation outside the loop:
```
int x = a * b;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    arr[i] = x + i;
}
```

blocks.prompt:
Consider the loop:
```
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    arr[i] = i * 2;
}
```
Apply strength reduction to optimize the multiplication.

steps.text:
Introduce a new variable to accumulate the result:
```
int x = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    arr[i] = x;
    x += 2;
}
```
